**Findings**
- P2: Per-segment recovery now applies the full `parse_bare_tool_calls` parser at every text flush, including its “truncated final call” repair path. [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1845) calls it on transition flushes from [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1870), but the parser treats unbalanced `{"name"...` to EOF as repairable at [api_common.h](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/api_common.h:661). That makes non-final segment boundaries behave like end-of-turn, so an incomplete call-shaped fragment before `<think>`/`<tool_call>` can be repaired and emitted via [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1856). This is a worse false-positive surface than the previous final-buffer scan and contradicts the “call split ACROSS segments stays surfaced as text” comment.

- P2: The malformed wrapped-call path is still a real coverage hole. In Responses non-stream, `!c.ok` commits `c.raw` directly as a message at [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1860) without running bare-call recovery. Chat and Anthropic instead append malformed raw text into `tx` before recovery at [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1362) and [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1545). A malformed wrapper containing a recoverable bare/nested call will be lost as message text here.

