- P1: none found.
- Definition order/captures are valid: `push_call` is defined before `flush_text`, and `items`, `tool_counter`, `custom_names`, `rn`, `tools`, and `msg_id` are all in scope around [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1809).
- For normal non-stream text segments with complete bare calls, `flush_text` clears once, emits pre-call prose first, then recovered call items, with no end-of-turn second recovery path: [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1829) and [metal_server.cpp](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/metal/metal_server.cpp:1891).
- The listed ordinary shapes avoid double-recovery/double-message, except for the malformed-wrapper hole above.
- Drift catalog logging is log-only; the parser logs after determining `out` and does not mutate the returned calls at [api_common.h](/Users/macthedan/projects/q27/src/api_common.h:780).

P3: none beyond the two P2s above.
